              "lv": "The child is sleeping."
            },
            {
              "de": "Es ist müde.",
              "lv": "It is tired."
            }
          ],
          "info": [
            "German es usually corresponds to English “it”.",
            "In weather expressions, English and German both use an impersonal subject."
          ],
          "comparison": [
            {
              "word": "es",
              "meaning": "it / impersonal subject",
